  "notes": [
    "Read as Latin-1 (FAO's encoding). Areas are M49 codes, placed through Natural Earth's UN_A3 (ISO_N3_EH where UN_A3 is missing: Norway, Taiwan); P3-11.",
    "A 3-year average such as 2023-2025 is stored with the year 2025, the last of its three; the range is in the period column.",
    "Values written \"<x\" are stored as x with the qualifier \"<x\" and shown \"under x%\" (ruling R3). Qualifiers seen: \"<2.5\" (1452 rows).",
    "Rows with no value (flag O, Q or L) are skipped, so a country's latest figure can be an older range than the newest in the file.",
    "Check: SDN undernourishment 10.9% (2020-2022).",
    "Check: YEM has no undernourishment figure in FAO's file (every range is missing).",
    "Check: HTI undernourishment 51.4% (2023-2025).",
    "Hand check 2026-11-23 (a separate script read the downloaded CSV, not the DataTool): all 329 values kept (country and item) equal the newest non-empty row for that M49 code; SDN 10.9% for 2020-2022 (2021-2023 to 2023-2025 flagged O, missing); HTI 51.4% for 2023-2025; YEM has no value in any range (all flagged O), so the Hunger layer leaves Yemen unshaded; CHN appears once (FAO 41, China mainland)."
  ]
